namespace SmSim.Extras.Warfront;

/// <summary>
/// Warfront (docs/added-content.md section 11): the persistent campaign on Musou Mode's battle. The one version of its rules, simulation and wire sections;
/// hashed into the config hash only under <see cref="ContentExtras.Warfront"/> (<c>SimConfig.ExtrasHash</c>), so raising it never touches another profile.
/// </summary>
public static class WarfrontRules
{
    /// <summary>26 (Chaos Warfront C4, the warp breaches: in a Chaos battle 1/2/3 breaches by lane node and 2 at the fortress approach send Daemon squads (5 every 20 s, at most 10 a breach and 30 in all) until one qualifying explosive of a human within 3 m closes one; a qualifying projectile detonates on a breach's 1.5 m sphere; the Chaos section, envelope tag 51; an Orks stage unchanged; renumbered at integration). 25 (Chaos Warfront C2, the Chaos roster on the sim: a Chaos stage's type table (Cultists, Traitor Guardsmen, Chaos Marines in the 'Ard Boy slot, the Aspiring Champion, Havocs, Raptors on the Stormboy code, the breach-only Daemon), no Weirdboyz, Meks or Squigs against Chaos, the caps at 0.6, the damage and stagger gate; an Orks stage unchanged; a hit not above 0 after the scales lands nothing; no wire change). 24 (the combined Chaos base, 2026-11-25: Chaos Warfront C1, owner brief 2026-11-24 rev 1: a run's army (Orks or Chaos) is chosen once at a new run by --warfront-faction alternate/orks/chaos, saved in run.json (SaveVersion 7) with the faction.json rotation beside it, and sent as the Hub's trailing faction byte, WarfrontWire.Format 3; Orks runs play unchanged). 23 (no squigs, owner 2026-11-25: "temporarily remove squigs from warfront mode"; <see cref="NoSquigs"/> stops the Bomb Squig drops in a Warfront battle; Musou Mode keeps them; no wire change). 22 (the weather finish, owner brief 2026-11-23: an active weather preset starts at full intensity and stays within 0.5 to 1, WeatherCatalog.Version 3; Clear is the authored look; presentation only, no wire change). 21 (codebase fix 6, owner 2026-11-22: a flying projectile (rokkit, launcher or plasma round) tests only an Ork's current pose, an instant shot keeps the 0.2 s trail; server hit rule, no wire change). 20 (codebase fix 1, owner 2026-11-22: a player's progression lives in his own progress.json and travels by the Progress command and the ProgressSave section, tag 49; the join catch-up grant is gone, a new player starts at level 1; stored levels top out at 50; WarfrontWire.Format 2). 19 (weather W2, owner 2026-11-21: Thunderstorm, Ash Squall and Ember Wind are built, forecast pool 2 adds the Thunderstorm for new campaigns, saves keep their stored forecast; presentation only, no wire change). 18 (weather W1, owner 2026-11-21: the weather catalog, the per-slot forecast in the save and the hub wire, the weather envelope tag 48 and command tag 43; presentation only). 17 (Guardsmen depth, owner 2026-11-20: twice the Guardsmen in every battle that has them, their health and damage scaled for an Orks-favoured balance, the squads in rows on a held point). 16 (retainer AI slice S1, owner 2026-11-19: a retainer's aim is the Classic bots' times 0.4 misses, targets are held and threats preferred, damage and health grow with the player's level like the Orks'). 15 (retainers: the squad AI follows MarineBrain.PlanRetainer, sight for every target; a Librarian's group is one uniform roll; an Assault/Raptor retainer fires its pistol at range; owner 2026-11-18). 14 (owner 2026-11-18: every level-up offer lists all five stat cards and +1 Retainer when eligible, the offer wire is 10 bytes; Warfront melee cleave reach x1.2, the Dreadnought x1.4, no target cap, Orks struck by collision). 13 (W13e: an Ork inside the ring it was sent to has arrived (WarfrontHeadwayNear); the allied pair only in solo lane battles; the fortress win tripwire; no home when already home). 12 (W14e: the fortress Warboss is put back on his spot when pinned on the way out or moved by Musou's failsafe). 11 (W13d: the allied AI Marine pair only when the server's human cap is one, the solo local campaign). 10 (W13c pass 2: no allied AI Marine pair on any Warfront map, HQ hold drains in 40 s, the HQ sight ray on the battle's rules). 9 (slice W13c: the HQ ramp foot fan and wall chamfer, level version 2, the rout rule, the HQ sight test). 8 (slice W14b: the fortress battle live on the arena, the final assault with one leashed Warboss, the stage flow, the win that leaves at once, the fortress HUD and messages). 7: the HQ defence second pass (W13b pass 2: the weighted hold fall rule, waves 200/300/400, Boss Orks with wave 2, alive cap 400, 10 spawns a tick, no Weirdboyz, the hold byte). 6: the HQ defence (slice W13b: its battle rules, survive 8 minutes, the Battle section tag 47, the elite share by node, the HQ composed with the hub). 5: the stage flow (slice W5a: supervisor, stage children, the hub/stage/down/results wire, identity, leader-only deploy, resume, end of run, squad and co-op wiring). 4: the card picker and XP HUD wire (slice W8, tags 44 and 45); W9b's squad wiring, stats feed and strength ruling ride on the same number until the lead renumbers. 3: the progression takes effect in a node battle (slice W3b: XP, level-up refill, the picker and its protection, the stat cards, Ork scaling by level, the AttackSpeedBonus field, the squad and stuck-log seams, assists). 2: the node battle rules and hook seams (slice W3: D as a capture point, no Warboss, the fallen human's spectator time and wipe rule, +20 % Ork health per extra human). 1: the switch and the skeleton (slice W1).</summary>
    public const uint Version = 26;

    /// <summary>
    /// The owner, 2026-11-25: "temporarily remove squigs from warfront mode" (ours, a temporary switch). True: no Bomb Squig spawns in a Warfront battle (the Squig drop director,
    /// <c>World.TfwSquigs.cs</c>, is Warfront's only squig source, and its capture aid's Squig goes with it); Musou Mode keeps its Squigs. Set false to restore them (and raise <see cref="Version"/>).
    /// </summary>
    public const bool NoSquigs = true;
}
